add_section('SECURITY.md','Category details and initial-session payload — September11','''Public wallet addresses can still reveal financial associations; typed detail fields and free Notes belong to the private planner record. Recipient SQL enumerates them only for an accepted Details grant, with current owner/person/matter and Never-disclose/revocation checks. Unknown JSON keys cannot broaden that projection; the negative DB-key test passes. Required field validation also applies to merged updates and approved maintenance changes. The minimum export and aggregate event metadata do not gain the new contents.

The native first-screen payload is created only after the existing identity/legal/session transaction succeeds. Its planner must match before the client uses it, and the opaque token is persisted first. Guest invitation lookup remains bounded metadata; registration returns to explicit acceptance with verified invited-email/account binding. No email-based account merge, extra provider secret or authentication bypass was introduced. The focused tests are recorded in the [QA report](output/qa/rillora-account-matter-ux-20260911/README.md); this is not a new full repository security audit.''')
add_section('docs/trust-safety-legal.md','September11 locator fields and Notes','''Crypto custody, network and a public wallet address locate an asset; they do not prove ownership, balance, access or authority. These fields and Notes are private data with explicit Details-level sharing. The form never asks for a private key, seed phrase, banking password or device unlock code. Free text is bounded and accompanied by concise guidance; this is not a claim that arbitrary secrets can be perfectly detected. No death/incapacity/unreachable or legal-release boundary changes. See [entry contract](account-matter-ux.md).''')
add_section('docs/start-here-export.md','September11 category-detail boundary','''New typed Matter details and Notes are deliberately absent from the minimum Start Here contents. They remain available only in the owner record and explicitly granted Details-level direct sharing. A changed matter still advances its source version and invalidates stale previews under the existing commitment rules. The current API test confirms that the wallet address and wallet-specific fields do not enter the minimum export or aggregate audit metadata; no cryptographic format or acknowledgement changes were made.''')
